    "primaryKeyword": "gutter cleaning Lynnwood WA",
    "html": "<h1>Gutter Cleaning in Lynnwood &amp; Snohomish County</h1>\n<p>Every fall in the Pacific Northwest, the same thing happens. Fir needles, maple leaves, and roof moss wash into the gutters, pack down into a wet sludge, and the first real rainstorm sends water spilling over the edge instead of down the downspout. That overflow ends up along your foundation, on your siding, and across your walkways.</p>\n<p>Cascade Clean Pros cleans gutters and downspouts for homeowners in <strong>Lynnwood and the surrounding Snohomish County area</strong>. We scoop out the debris by hand, flush the gutters, make sure every downspout drains, and haul the mess away with us. No guesswork, no mess left in your flower beds.</p>\n<h2>Fall intro pricing</h2>\n<p>We&#39;ve added gutter cleaning to our services this fall, with intro pricing for the season:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One-story home: $99</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Two-story home: $149</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Roof debris removal add-on: +$50 to $75</strong> (needles and leaves blown or brushed off low-pitch roofs, when the roof is dry and safe to work)</li>\n<li><strong>Three-story homes, very large homes, or badly clogged gutters:</strong> we&#39;ll give you an exact price before we start</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Intro pricing is for our first 10 gutter cleanings this fall. Call or text <strong>(360) 202-7249</strong> to lock in your spot.</p>\n<h2>What&#39;s included</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hand removal of leaves, needles, moss, and packed debris from all gutters</li>\n<li>A water flush to confirm the gutters drain toward the downspouts</li>\n<li>Downspouts checked and cleared so water actually leaves the gutter</li>\n<li>All debris bagged and hauled away, with tarps down to protect your yard and landscaping</li>\n<li>Before and after photos so you can see the result without climbing a ladder</li>\n<li>A heads-up on anything we notice, like loose hangers, leaking seams, or moss on the roof</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our 30-day overflow guarantee</h2>\n<p>If your gutters overflow within 30 days because of something we missed, we&#39;ll come back and fix it free. Simple as that.</p>\n<h2>Why fall gutter cleaning matters here</h2>\n<p>Western Washington gets most of its rain from October through March, and that&#39;s exactly when trees drop the most debris. Clogged gutters during the wet season can lead to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Water pouring over the edge and pooling along your foundation</li>\n<li>Soaked fascia boards and soffits, which can start to rot over time</li>\n<li>Staining and algae streaks down your siding</li>\n<li>Slick, mossy walkways and steps below overflowing gutters</li>\n<li>Heavy gutters pulling loose from the house</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Most homes around here do well with a cleaning in <strong>late fall</strong>, after the leaves are down, and many homes with tall firs nearby benefit from a second cleaning in <strong>spring</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Pair it with other exterior cleaning</h2>\n<p>Since we&#39;re already at your house, gutter cleaning pairs well with our other services:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/services/roof-cleaning/\">Roof cleaning and moss treatment</a>, since moss on the roof is one of the biggest sources of gutter clogs</li>\n<li><a href=\"/services/house-washing/\">House washing</a> to clear the black streaks that overflowing gutters leave behind</li>\n<li><a href=\"/services/driveway-concrete-cleaning/\">Driveway and concrete cleaning</a> for walkways that turn slick and green in the wet season</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ask about bundling when you call.</p>\n<h2>Gutter cleaning FAQ</h2>\n<p><strong>Do I need to be home?</strong>\nNo. As long as we can get to all sides of the house and use an outdoor spigot, we can do the job while you&#39;re out. We&#39;ll text you the before and after photos.</p>\n<p><strong>How long does it take?</strong>\nMost one-story and two-story homes take one to two hours, depending on size and how packed the gutters are.</p>\n<p><strong>What happens to the debris?</strong>\nWe bag it and take it with us. We put tarps down under the work area so it doesn&#39;t end up in your lawn or flower beds.</p>\n<p><strong>How often should gutters be cleaned in Western Washington?</strong>\nAt least once a year, in late fall. Homes surrounded by firs or big maples often need a second cleaning in spring.</p>\n<p><strong>Do you repair gutters?</strong>\nOur focus is cleaning. If we spot loose hangers, leaking seams, or damage, we&#39;ll show you photos and can point you toward someone for the repair.</p>\n<p><strong>How do I pay?</strong>\nPayment is due when the job is done. We take cash, and we&#39;re happy to walk you through the photos first.</p>\n<p><strong>Book gutter cleaning:</strong> call or text <strong>(360) 202-7249</strong>, or email <strong><a href=\"mailto:info@cascadecleanpros.com\">info@cascadecleanpros.com</a></strong>.</p>\n<h2>Where we provide gutter cleaning</h2>\n<p>We clean gutters in <a href=\"/locations/lynnwood-wa/\">Lynnwood</a> and nearby communities, including Edmonds, <a href=\"/locations/mill-creek-wa/\">Mill Creek</a>, Mountlake Terrace, Bothell, Mukilteo, and <a href=\"/locations/everett-wa/\">Everett</a>. Not sure if you&#39;re in our area? Just ask.</p>"
